WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
- All right! I love scrolling
through the infinite pages

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.880
of social media to find the
stuff that makes us all smile,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.150
and I love sharing it with you all.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.580
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.427
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.427 --> 00:00:14.420
A woman in Stockholm, Sweden
has an unusual obsession

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.390
with a simple household item: safety pins.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:18.400
And she's awesome.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.870
And she makes fully functional
fashion pieces you can wear,

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.100
all with those little metal objects.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.590
Here's a mask, which is so cool.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:29.480
Here's a dress to match, 'cause why not?

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.845
And this is the artist wearing
one of her handmade jackets.

00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:33.678
(audience gasps)

00:00:33.678 --> 00:00:34.940
I know, see all the oohs, ahhs.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.850
All those were good.
They were (indistinct)

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:37.800
It's how you feel.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.063
She's put together her first collection,

00:00:40.063 --> 00:00:41.830
she calls it Obsession.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.440
And I'll tell you, I am obsessed.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.330
It's such a talent.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.570
Let's get Tonio on the line right now.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.971
All right, what's on Tonio?

00:00:47.971 --> 00:00:49.245
(audience applause)

00:00:49.245 --> 00:00:50.740
- Hi

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.880
- Okay, so why, why safety
pins, I have to ask you?

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.530
It's lovely to meet you as well.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.250
- Well, I just love
using an everyday object

00:00:58.250 --> 00:00:59.350
and transforming it into

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.200
something completely different.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.260
To put it in a situation.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:06.950
It gets it to show off its beauty and

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.680
just transform it to something else.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.490
And put it in a context where it's not

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.280
supposed to be, very unexpected.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.600
And it's like kind of
a modern day pop art.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.960
And I also love how shiny
the metal pieces are.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:21.880
A few years ago,

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.430
I actually watched a lot of
Project Runway, and I felt

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.590
inspired to do my own
unconventional challenge.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.010
So I ended up buying hundred
thousand safety pins,

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.012
and 500 hours after that,

00:01:34.012 --> 00:01:37.160
I had created my first creation ever.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.980
Which I ended up giving
away to a good cause.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:40.813
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:40.813 --> 00:01:41.646
It's so cool.

00:01:41.646 --> 00:01:43.830
Reminds me, I don't
know if you saw Cruella?

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:44.780
The new Cruella?

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.660
But it reminds me of all those
dresses that like make on

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:47.760
that show. It's so inspiring.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.850
It's so cool.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.460
Can you tell us about
your Obsession collection?

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.293
- Yeah.

00:01:52.293 --> 00:01:56.300
My collection contains 10
outfits and took 7,000 hours to

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.490
complete during one year.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.160
It's called Obsession because it

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.320
was such an obsession.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.200
I could not stop working with it

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.920
and it actually consumed me a little bit.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.550
But I do love this art form and

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.340
I would love to do it full time.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.870
So recently last year I
quit my full-time job as a

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.277
visual designer to pursue this
dream, to become an artist.

00:02:17.277 --> 00:02:21.216
So now I'm hoping that I will
be able to support myself as

00:02:21.216 --> 00:02:22.840
an artist in the future.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.730
And I would love to travel
the world and have exhibitions

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:29.960
showcasing my artwork and
my avant garde fashion.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.470
- Oh my God. Well man,
good luck to you, Tonio.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.940
It's amazing.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.310
It's truly, really cool.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.726
Like what you're doing and I've
never seen anything like it.

00:02:36.726 --> 00:02:38.965
I'm liking your post right now. Right?

00:02:38.965 --> 00:02:41.450
All right?

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.283
All right,

00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:44.500
Well that's not all our
season long partner pilot pin,

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.930
the go-to pin to the Kelly
Clarkson show likes to celebrate

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.680
those who create fearlessly,
just like you ma'am.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.940
So they're going to be using
their friction erasable pen to

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.810
write you a check for a thousand dollars.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.379
How's that sound?

00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:56.290
(audience applause)

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.550
You can buy, a ton of safety pins.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:00.793
With a thousand dollars.

